# MEMORY.md — {{ profile.name }}

> _Memory layout for the RAG agent. Three layers: session, persistent, skill-derived._

## Layer 1 — Session memory

Per-conversation state. Lives in the agent runtime; not persisted.

Schema: `.harness/memory_schemas/conversation.json`

```jsonc
{
  "messages": [{ "role": "user" | "assistant", "content": "...", "ts": "..." }],
  "retrieved_chunks": [{"chunk_id": "...", "score": 0.0, "used_in_turn": 1}]
}
```

## Layer 2 — Persistent corpus

The indexed document chunks. Lives in the vector store (Qdrant / Chroma /
Postgres-pgvector). Re-indexable from source.

Schema: `.harness/memory_schemas/rag_chunks.json`

```jsonc
{
  "chunk_id": "<stable-hash>",
  "source": "<file or URL>",
  "text": "...",
  "embedding": [0.0, ...],
  "metadata": {"section": "...", "page": 0, "indexed_at": "..."}
}
```

## Layer 3 — Skill-derived memory

When a skill (`SKILLS/<name>/SKILL.md`) produces a reusable artifact
(e.g. a learned chunking heuristic, a tuned rerank threshold), it
writes to:

```
.harness/skill_memory/<skill-name>/<artifact>.json
```

This is the only memory the agent should *create* on its own.

## Retention policy

- Session memory: discarded when the conversation closes.
- Persistent corpus: rebuilt on `./scripts/test_task.sh --reindex`.
- Skill memory: kept across sessions; archived on `harness sync --force`.
- **Never** persist user PII without an explicit opt-in event in session memory.

## Forbidden

- Do not embed secrets, env values, or anything from `{{ profile.forbidden_paths | join(", ") }}` into the vector store.
- Do not write to `.harness/memory_schemas/` — that's the schema, not data.
